# Docker matches these against context-root-relative paths, so a bare name only
# ever means the top-level one. `node_modules` and `.env` were doing exactly
# that: ui/node_modules was uploaded and then COPYed over the image's own
# `npm ci` output (host binaries into a Linux image), and server/.env — which
# holds SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY, DAYTONA_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY and
# OYA_PROFILE_SECRET — went into the build context on every build.
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/dist
.git
*.log
.DS_Store
extension
.claude
README.md
